  "major": "Biology: Pre-Physical Therapy Concentration",
  "notes": "Term-by-term curriculum as printed in the 2023-2024 ASU Undergraduate Catalog (Dept. of Biological Sciences). Generalized curriculum preparing students for competitive admission to Doctor of Physical Therapy programs; course substitutions require curriculum advisor approval. Physical therapy schools differ in prerequisites — students should consult advisors and target programs. After completing the degree plan and passing a Departmental Comprehensive (exit) Examination, the student receives the B.S. Degree in Biology with a pre-physical therapy concentration. Suggested restricted electives: BI 361 with lab, BI 402, BI 446 with lab, or others with advisor/chair approval (catalog p.173).",
